(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the 'Strangler Fig Pattern' \(Martin Fowler\) as an architectural strategy for software redesign. How does it de-risk enterprise platform migrations compared to high-risk 'Big-Bang' rewrites?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Australian Strangler Fig Analogy:) Tj
T*
(   - The strangler fig seed germinates in the upper canopy of an established host tree, slowly) Tj
T*
(   sending aerial roots down to the forest floor. Over decades, the fig roots thicken, gradually) Tj
T*
(   enveloping and replacing the original host tree until the host rots away, leaving an) Tj
T*
(   independent, magnificent fig tree standing in its place.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Catastrophic Pathology of Big-Bang Rewrites \(The Second-System Effect\):) Tj
T*
(   - An enterprise attempts to rewrite an aging 10-year-old monolith from scratch in a new tech) Tj
T*
(   stack \(e.g., Go/Kubernetes\).) Tj
T*
(   - Pathology: The rewrite takes 3 years instead of 1 year. During those 3 years, the legacy) Tj
T*
(   monolith continues to evolve, adding new features. The new system is chasing a moving target.) Tj
T*
(   When the 'big-bang cutover' occurs over a weekend, unpredicted edge cases trigger catastrophic) Tj
T*
(   global outages, forcing emergency rollbacks and incinerating millions in capital.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Step-by-Step Strangler Fig Engineering Pipeline:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Intercept at the Gateway: Deploy an intelligent Ingress API Gateway \(e.g., Envoy /) Tj
T*
(   Kong\) in front of the legacy monolith. All user traffic flows through the gateway to the) Tj
T*
(   monolith.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Implement a Single Modular Slice: Engineer a new microservice that handles a single) Tj
T*
(   specific domain capability \(e.g., 'User Authentication'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Divert Traffic Incrementally: The API gateway redirects `/auth/*` traffic to the new) Tj
T*
(   microservice, while all other routes continue hitting the monolith.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: Iterative Strangulation: Repeat process endpoint by endpoint \(Billing, Search,) Tj
T*
(   Inventory\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: Decommission the Shell: Once 100% of routes are served by new services, the legacy) Tj
T*
(   monolith is powered off with zero user downtime and zero operational risk.) Tj
T*
ET

