(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the 'Architecture Decision Record' \(ADR\) framework. Write a comprehensive, production-grade ADR documenting an architectural decision to migrate from a REST API architecture to GraphQL.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Context and Purpose of Architecture Decision Records \(ADRs\):) Tj
T*
(   - Created by Michael Nygard, ADRs capture the context, trade-offs, and rationale behind) Tj
T*
(   foundational engineering choices, preserving institutional memory and onboarding future) Tj
T*
(   developers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Comprehensive Production-Grade ADR Document:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # ADR-042: Migration of Mobile Client Data Layer from REST to GraphQL) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ## Status:) Tj
T*
(   ACCEPTED [Date: 2026-10-26 | Author: Senior Systems Architect]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ## Context:) Tj
T*
(   Our mobile application currently communicates with backend services via 35 disparate REST) Tj
T*
(   endpoints. On 3G cellular connections in emerging markets, loading the primary dashboard) Tj
T*
(   requires the mobile client to execute 8 sequential HTTP round-trips, suffering from severe) Tj
T*
(   'Over-Fetching' \(downloading 400KB of unneeded JSON fields\) and 'Under-Fetching' \(forcing) Tj
T*
(   secondary waterfall requests\). This contributes to a 4.2-second initial screen load latency and) Tj
T*
(   a 22% customer drop-off rate during onboarding.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ## Decision:) Tj
T*
(   We will deploy an Apollo GraphQL Federation gateway layer in front of our backend) Tj
T*
(   microservices. Mobile clients will query the federated GraphQL schema, requesting exactly and) Tj
T*
(   only the specific fields required for each screen in a single HTTP POST round-trip.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ## Evaluated Alternatives:) Tj
T*
(   1. Maintain REST and build custom composite BFF \(Backend-For-Frontend\) REST endpoints: Rejected) Tj
T*
(   due to severe endpoint proliferation and high maintenance overhead for every UI variant.) Tj
T*
(   2. Migrate to gRPC-Web: Rejected because gRPC binary payloads lack flexible client-driven field) Tj
T*
(   selection and impose steep browser tooling friction.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ## Consequences:) Tj
T*
(   - Positive Consequences:) Tj
T*
(   * Slashes mobile network payload sizes by 68% \(from 400KB to 128KB\).) Tj
T*
(   * Reduces client dashboard load latency from 4.2s to 850ms in 3G networks.) Tj
T*
(   * Decouples frontend UI component iterations from backend database schema updates.) Tj
T*
(   - Negative Consequences & Mitigations \(Accepted Technical Debt\):) Tj
T*
(   * Increases backend gateway computational complexity: mitigated by enforcing query depth limits) Tj
T*
(   \(max depth = 5\) to prevent malicious nested query DoS attacks.) Tj
T*
(   * Complex HTTP response caching: mitigated by implementing persisted queries and Redis edge) Tj
T*
(   caching based on operation hashes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
