(   2. The Product Trio Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Teresa Torres reframes the atomic unit of product innovation as the 'Product Trio': the) Tj
T*
(   Product Manager, the Lead UX Designer, and the Lead Software Engineer collaborating as an) Tj
T*
(   equal, co-creative unit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The Weekly Touchpoint Ritual:) Tj
T*
(   - The Trio conducts at least one joint user interview and usability test every single week.) Tj
T*
(   - Direct Engineering Exposure: By having the software engineer physically observe real) Tj
T*
(   customers struggling with API errors, sluggish screens, and confusing terminology, the engineer) Tj
T*
(   develops deep visceral empathy.) Tj
T*
(   - Real-Time Feasibility Collaboration: When a user requests a capability during an interview,) Tj
T*
(   the engineer immediately chimes in with creative technological possibilities \('We can use) Tj
T*
(   WebSocket server-sent events to make that update instantaneously at zero server cost!'\).) Tj
T*
(   - Eliminates PRDs: Specifications are replaced by shared mental models, rapid prototype spikes,) Tj
T*
(   and continuous, collaborative learning.) Tj
