(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Maurya's Rationale for Adapting the Canvas:) Tj
T*
(   - Osterwalder's original Business Model Canvas was architected for established enterprises,) Tj
T*
(   emphasizing Key Partners, Key Activities, and Key Resources.) Tj
T*
(   - For an early-stage startup, these components are largely hypothetical distractions. Ash) Tj
T*
(   Maurya replaced them with high-risk, volatile components: Problem, Solution, Key Metrics, and) Tj
T*
(   Unfair Advantage.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Deconstruction of the Nine Lean Canvas Building Blocks:) Tj
T*
(   - Block 1: Problem: Top 3 urgent problems experienced by customers \(plus existing) Tj
T*
(   alternatives\).) Tj
T*
(   - Block 2: Customer Segments: Target users and early adopters.) Tj
T*
(   - Block 3: Unique Value Proposition: Single, clear, compelling message stating why you are) Tj
T*
(   different and worth paying for.) Tj
T*
(   - Block 4: Solution: Top 3 features that directly solve the top 3 problems.) Tj
T*
(   - Block 5: Channels: Scalable pathways to customer acquisition.) Tj
T*
(   - Block 6: Revenue Streams: Monetization model, pricing, and lifetime value.) Tj
T*
(   - Block 7: Cost Structure: Customer acquisition costs, server hosting, and salaries.) Tj
T*
(   - Block 8: Key Metrics: The core numbers indicating business health \(AARRR: Pirate Metrics\).) Tj
T*
(   - Block 9: Unfair Advantage: The defensible moat that cannot easily be copied or bought) Tj
T*
(   \(proprietary algorithms, exclusive data, network effects\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Agile Iteration Instrument:) Tj
T*
(   - The Lean Canvas is treated as a living, disposable hypothesis sheet updated after every) Tj
T*
(   customer interview sprint.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
