(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the 'Three Horizons of Growth' framework \(McKinsey & Co.\) applied to organizational product innovation and continuous redesign.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Three Horizons Architectural Topology:) Tj
T*
(   - Developed by Baghai, Coley, and White, this framework balances immediate operational survival) Tj
T*
(   with future transformative breakthrough innovation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Operational Definitions across Horizons:) Tj
T*
(   - Horizon 1 \(H1: Core Business Optimization - 70% of Resources\):) Tj
T*
(   * Focus: Extending, defending, and optimizing existing core products.) Tj
T*
(   * Design Activity: Incremental redesign, UX bug squashing, performance optimizations, and) Tj
T*
(   design system component refactoring. Generates current cash flow.) Tj
T*
(   - Horizon 2 \(H2: Emerging Opportunities & Adjacent Markets - 20% of Resources\):) Tj
T*
(   * Focus: Scaling promising new ventures, expanding into adjacent customer segments, or) Tj
T*
(   launching major new platform capabilities.) Tj
T*
(   * Design Activity: Medium-fidelity prototyping, customer segment pivots, and integrating) Tj
T*
(   third-party APIs. Expected to generate major revenue in 2-3 years.) Tj
T*
(   - Horizon 3 \(H3: Transformational Moonshots - 10% of Resources\):) Tj
T*
(   * Focus: Long-term disruptive bets, breakthrough technologies, and entirely novel business) Tj
T*
(   paradigms.) Tj
T*
(   * Design Activity: Radical exploratory research, blue-sky prototyping, and speculative design.) Tj
T*
(   Prepares the organization for market dominance in 5-10 years.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Strategic Synergy:) Tj
T*
(   - Companies that focus exclusively on H1 face sudden disruption when technological paradigms) Tj
T*
(   shift; companies that chase only H3 run out of cash before shipping anything.) Tj
T*
