(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the 'Cognitive Ergonomics of Design Handoffs'. How do modern tools like Storybook, Figma Dev Mode, and Design Systems eliminate ambiguity for globally distributed software teams?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Chronic Friction of Historical Design Handoffs:) Tj
T*
(   - Historically, UI designers delivered static 2D image exports \(PNG/PDF\) with handwritten) Tj
T*
(   margin annotations.) Tj
T*
(   - The Cognitive Ambiguity: Static images fail to communicate responsive breakpoint behaviors,) Tj
T*
(   hover transitions, error states, dynamic text wrapping, and keyboard accessibility focus rings.) Tj
T*
(   Developers were forced to guess, leading to massive design-code divergence and frustrating) Tj
T*
(   sprint rework.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Modern Component-Driven Engineering Handoff:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Figma Dev Mode & Interactive Variables:) Tj
T*
(   * Developers inspect direct CSS variables, typography tokens, and responsive auto-layout) Tj
T*
(   constraints directly in the design file, eliminating manual ruler measurements.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: The Storybook Component Sandbox:) Tj
T*
(   * An isolated, interactive development environment where UI components \(buttons, modals,) Tj
T*
(   tables\) are rendered in all permissible states \(loading, empty, disabled, error\) using real) Tj
T*
(   production code.) Tj
T*
(   * Product managers, designers, and QA engineers can test edge cases \(e.g., a 200-character) Tj
T*
(   username\) inside Storybook before the component is integrated into the core application.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Automated Visual Regression Testing \(Chromatic\):) Tj
T*
(   * Automated CI/CD pipelines screenshot components across browsers, flagging any unintended) Tj
T*
(   1-pixel shift before code merges into master.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
